INT. QUARANTINED CRUISE SHIP - GIFT SHOP - NIGHT

Shelves of magnets, snow globes, sunscreen. The registers are dark. Emergency strips light the floor. Through the glass storefront, an empty promenade deck rocks gently at anchor.

RENATA KOVAC, 40s, ship's purser, hair in a messy bun, uniform jacket unbuttoned, sits behind the counter with a radio on her knee. MILES TOBIN, 30s, ship's doctor, mask around his chin, leans on a shelf. ADEBAYO ROSS, 50s, passenger, bathrobe, paper slippers, pretends to read a paperback.

The radio crackles.

CAPTAIN HALE (V.O.)
Shop, this is the bridge. Status.

RENATA
(into radio)
Three souls, sir. All calm.

CAPTAIN HALE (V.O.)
Keep them there. We've got a boat coming at dawn.

RENATA
Understood.

She sets the radio down. The silence returns.

ADEBAYO
(to no one)
Two weeks on a boat, and the one thing they sell me is snow globes.

MILES
You can have mine.

ADEBAYO
Does it come with a cure?

MILES
It comes with a mild placebo effect.

Adebayo laughs, then coughs. Miles straightens, watches him.

MILES (CONT'D)
(quietly)
Sir, how long has that been going?

ADEBAYO
It's a tickle.

MILES
How long?

ADEBAYO
Since Tuesday.

Renata stiffens. She slides her hand slowly toward the radio.

RENATA
(to all)
Everyone stay exactly where you are.

MILES
Renata.

RENATA
Don't.

MILES
He's not necessarily--

RENATA
You said no one on this deck was symptomatic.

Miles opens his mouth. Closes it.

ADEBAYO
(muttering)
I should've stayed in the cabin.

The storefront lights flicker. Outside, a searchlight sweeps the promenade. Then a second. Then a third, from a hull that isn't theirs.

RENATA
That's not the dawn boat.

MILES
No.

She lifts the radio.

RENATA (CONT'D)
Bridge, we have lights on the promenade.

Static. Nothing. She tries again.

RENATA (CONT'D)
Bridge?

CAPTAIN HALE (V.O.)
(whispering)
Don't open the door. They're not ours.
